===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|en|braunch||obsolete}}

===Etymology===
[[File:Acacia constricta branch.jpg|thumb|Tree branches]]
{{dercat|en|cel}}
From {{inh|en|enm|branche}}, {{m|enm|braunche}}, {{m|enm|bronche}}, from {{der|en|fro|branche}}, {{m|fro|branke}}, from {{der|en|LL.|branca|t=footprint”, later also “paw, claw}} (whence {{cog|gmh|pranke}}, {{cog|de|Pranke|t=paw}}), of {{unk|en|title=unknown}} origin.

Perhaps of {{der|en|cel|-}} origin, from a hypothetical {{der|en|cel-gau|*vranca}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro||*wrónk-eh₂}}.<ref>{{R:American_Heritage_Dictionary|branch}}</ref> If so, then Indo-European cognates include {{cog|non|rá}}, {{m|non|vró|t=angle, corner}}, and possibly {{cog|lt|rankà|t=hand}}, {{cog|cu|рѫка|t=hand}}, {{cog|sq|rangë|t=yardwork}}.

The verb is from {{inh|en|enm|braunchen}}, from the noun.

